  "details": "Vrchat version: build 751, on windows 10\n\nDescription:\n\nSince a few days ago, entering urls, using video controls, and other rpc events used for video players do not seem to have any effect to me when I try to instigate them. if someone else is in the instance, the commands i send seem to happen on their client. if i leave the room, making the other person master of the instance, and come back, i can see the video of the url entered, whether it is still the one i entered, or a new one they entered. sometimes, possibly not always, it seems that in addition to this problem, if the master of the instance (who isn't me) sends an rpc like play, pause, or stop, the video follows the command on other clients like normal, but for me, the video ignores the command, and keeps playing on my client if the command was supposed to stop it, for example. I have restarted my computer, cleared my cache, and deleted the registry for vrchat, and i have tested the issue in multiple worlds with video players, on both the stream and the video player, the problem persists.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\nIt seems to be limited only to my account and/or client or possibly select others, but otherwise; 1) enter instance of world with a video or stream player with at least one other person, be master of the instance, 2) enter url, see if it works and for who, 3) leave instance and come back, or make new instance with a different player as master, 4) have master try entering a new url, and using the play/pause/stop/next/previous commands",
